        "original_id": "f4505a30-5666-50c7-84cb-0a7b2bc6825e",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Organizations: Vanderbilt University, Bowdoin College, Kentucky Wesleyan College, Methodist Church, MIT\n- People: Cornelius Vanderbilt, John Wesley Hughes, Todd Siler\n- Places: Brunswick, Maine, Massachusetts, Millersburg, Kentucky, Owensboro, Kentucky, Nashville, Tennessee\n- Topics: founding, chartering, education, endowment\n\nFacts:\n- Bowdoin College was chartered in 1794, when Maine was still part of the Commonwealth of Massachusetts.\n- Vanderbilt University was founded in 1873 and was named in honor of Cornelius Vanderbilt.\n- Cornelius Vanderbilt provided Vanderbilt University with its initial $1 million endowment despite never having been to the South.\n- Bowdoin College is a private liberal arts college located in Brunswick, Maine.\n- John Wesley Hughes attended Kentucky Wesleyan College in Millersburg, Kentucky, which is now located in Owensboro, Kentucky.\n- John Wesley Hughes served as a pastor in the Kentucky Conference of the Methodist Church before pursuing further education at Vanderbilt University in Nashville, Tennessee.\n- Todd Siler graduated from Bowdoin College.\n- Todd Siler became the first visual artist to receive a PhD from MIT in interdisciplinary studies in Psychology and Art in 1986.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "32b3bd7a-869c-5f87-b342-79ca186a06e5",
        "text": "Page: Vanderbilt University. Sentence: Founded in 1873, it was named in honor of shipping and rail magnate Cornelius Vanderbilt, who provided the school its initial $1 million endowment despite having never been to the South.\nPage: Bowdoin College. Sentence: Bowdoin College ( ) is a private liberal arts college located in Brunswick, Maine.\nPage: Bowdoin College. Sentence: At the time Bowdoin was chartered in 1794, Maine was still a part of the Commonwealth of Massachusetts.\nPage: John Wesley Hughes. Sentence: Hughes attended Kentucky Wesleyan College in Millersburg, Kentucky (now located in Owensboro, Kentucky), and served as a pastor in the Kentucky Conference of the Methodist Church before pursuing further education at Vanderbilt University in Nashville, Tennessee.\nPage: Todd Siler. Sentence: A graduate of Bowdoin College, he became the first visual artist to be granted a PhD from MIT (interdisciplinary studies in Psychology and Art, 1986).",
